## Tech Stack
- Language: Kotlin
- UI: Jetpack Compose
- Architecture: MVVM + Clean Architecture
- DI: Hilt
- Async: Coroutines + Flow
- Navigation: Compose Navigation
- Min SDK: 26
- Target SDK: 34

## Project Structure
```
app/
  src/
    main/
      java/com/yourpackage/
        data/          ← Repository layer, data sources
        domain/        ← Use cases, models
        ui/            ← ViewModels, Compose screens
          screens/     ← One folder per screen
          components/  ← Shared composables
        di/            ← Hilt modules
```

## Code Conventions
- ViewModels live in ui/screens/<FeatureName>/
- Never put business logic in Composables
- Use StateFlow for UI state, not LiveData
- All network calls go through repository layer
- Error handling: use sealed Result<T> classes
- String resources in res/values/strings.xml (never hardcode)

## Agent-Specific Rules
- NEVER modify build.gradle.kts without running a build to verify
- NEVER change minSdk or targetSdk
- NEVER add dependencies without checking for conflicts first
- Always run ./gradlew assembleDebug before marking a task done
- Always write/update unit tests for any logic you change
- Commit message format: "Fix #<issue>: <short description>"
